.*
.* WRKSBSD: the subsystem descriptions a name selects. The first entry
.* is blank: option 1 there creates one.
:PNLGRP.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=TEXTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 50'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=SBSD CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=SBSDLIB CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=SBSDTEXT CLASS=TEXTCL.
:LISTDEF NAME=SBSDS VARS='OPT SBSD SBSDLIB SBSDTEXT'.
:KEYL NAME=SDKEYS HELP='KEYS/SDKEYS'.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F11 ACTION='RETURN 11'.F11=Display names only
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F16 ACTION='RETURN 16'.F16=Repeat position to
:KEYI KEY=F17 ACTION='RETURN 17'.F17=Position to
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKSBSD KEYL=SDKEYS HELP=WRKSBSD ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SPACE.Work with Subsystem Descriptions
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=SBSDS VIEWS=2 EXTACT=YES.(No subsystem descriptions selected)
:LISTACT OPTION=1 ACTFOR=EXTACT ENTER='RETURN 1' HELP='WRKSBSD/OPTIONS'.1=Create
:LISTACT OPTION=2 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD ?CHGSBSD SBSD(&SBSDLIB./&SBSD.)' HELP='WRKSBSD/OPTIONS'.2=Change
:LISTACT OPTION=4 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD ?DLTSBSD SBSD(&SBSDLIB./&SBSD.)' HELP='WRKSBSD/OPTIONS'.4=Delete
:LISTACT OPTION=5 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD DSPSBSD SBSD(&SBSDLIB./&SBSD.)' HELP='WRKSBSD/OPTIONS'.5=Display
:LISTACT OPTION=8 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD WRKSBSJOB SBS(&SBSD.)' HELP='WRKSBSD/OPTIONS'.8=Work with subsystem jobs
:LISTACT OPTION=9 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD STRSBS SBSD(&SBSDLIB./&SBSD.)' HELP='WRKSBSD/OPTIONS'.9=Start subsystem
:LISTACT OPTION=10 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD ?ENDSBS SBS(&SBSD.)' HELP='WRKSBSD/OPTIONS'.10=End subsystem
:LISTCOL VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT HELP='WRKSBSD/OPT'.Opt
:LISTCOL VAR=SBSD USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES HELP='FLD/SBSD'.Subsystem
:LISTCOL VAR=SBSDLIB USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES HELP='FLD/SBSDLIB'.Library
:LISTCOL VAR=SBSDTEXT USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/SBSDTEXT'.Text
:LISTVIEW COLS='OPT SBSD SBSDLIB SBSDTEXT'.
:LISTVIEW COLS='OPT SBSD SBSDLIB'.
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.Parameters for options 1, 2, 5, 8 and 10 or command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=WRKSBSD.Work with Subsystem Descriptions - Help
:P.The subsystem descriptions the name selects. Type an option next to
one to change, display, start or end it; option 1 on the blank first
line creates one with the name typed on the command line.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/SDKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F4=Prompt
:PD.Prompts the command on the command line, or the command of the
option typed.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F9=Retrieve
:PD.Puts the last command run back on the command line; press it again
for the one before.
:PT.F11=Display names only
:PD.Shows the list with the names alone, so more fit on a page.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F16=Repeat position to
:PD.Repeat position to.
:PT.F17=Position to
:PD.Positions the list at the name typed on the command line.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKSBSD/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SBSD'.Subsystem
:P.The subsystem of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SBSDLIB'.Library
:P.The library of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SBSDTEXT'.Text
:P.The text of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKSBSD/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.1=Create
:PD.Type 1 next to an entry and press Enter to create it.
:PT.2=Change
:PD.Type 2 next to an entry and press Enter to change it. The Change
Subsystem Description (CHGSBSD) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.4=Delete
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to delete it. The Delete
Subsystem Description (DLTSBSD) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.5=Display
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display it. The Display
Subsystem Description (DSPSBSD) command runs for the entry.
:PT.8=Work with subsystem jobs
:PD.Type 8 next to an entry and press Enter to work with subsystem jobs
it. The Work with Subsystem Jobs (WRKSBSJOB) command runs for the entry.
:PT.9=Start subsystem
:PD.Type 9 next to an entry and press Enter to start subsystem it. The
Start Subsystem (STRSBS) command runs for the entry.
:PT.10=End subsystem
:PD.Type 10 next to an entry and press Enter to end subsystem it. The
End Subsystem (ENDSBS) command is prompted for the entry.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
